{
  "date": "2026-11-27",
  "pillar": "Technology & Architecture",
  "headline": "Deploying code and releasing a feature are two different decisions.",
  "slides": [
    {
      "theme": "dark",
      "tag": "Architecture · Delivery",
      "offset": 170,
      "html": "<h1 style='font-size:104px'>Deploy is a technical event.</h1><h1 class='accent' style='font-size:104px;margin-top:28px'>Release is a business decision.</h1><p style='margin-top:52px;max-width:820px'>When one button does both, every launch is a gamble and every rollback is an emergency.</p>",
      "footnote": "swipe →"
    },
    {
      "theme": "light",
      "tag": "Context",
      "offset": 130,
      "html": "<div class='kicker'>The coupled launch</div><h2>Merge, deploy, and hope.</h2><p>In many teams, the moment code reaches production is the moment every user sees it.</p><hr><p style='color:#0E0E0E'>So launches wait for a quiet window. Big changes pile up in one risky deploy.</p><p style='margin-top:18px'>And when something breaks, the only way back is another deploy, under pressure, with customers watching.</p>"
    },
    {
      "theme": "light",
      "tag": "The concept",
      "offset": 120,
      "html": "<div class='kicker'>Separate the two</div><h2>Ship the code dark. Turn it on later.</h2><p><b style='font-family:Space Grotesk'>Deploy:</b> the new code is running in production.</p><hr style='margin:26px 0'><p><b style='font-family:Space Grotesk'>Release:</b> users can actually reach it.</p><hr style='margin:26px 0'><p><b style='font-family:Space Grotesk'>Feature flag:</b> a runtime switch between the two. Changed by configuration, <span class='accent'>not by a new build</span>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "theme": "light",
      "tag": "How it works",
      "offset": 100,
      "html": "<h2 style='margin-bottom:26px'>One deploy. A release in steps.</h2><svg width='850' height='800' viewBox='0 0 850 800'><g font-family='Plex Mono'><line x1='30' y1='40' x2='30' y2='590' stroke='#D4D4D0' stroke-width='3'/><rect x='20' y='30' width='20' height='20' fill='#0E0E0E'/><text x='70' y='48' font-size='27' font-weight='500' fill='#0E0E0E'>DEPLOY</text><text x='70' y='84' font-size='22' fill='#6B6B6B'>code in production · flag OFF</text><rect x='20' y='140' width='20' height='20' fill='#2F5FE8'/><text x='70' y='158' font-size='27' font-weight='500' fill='#0E0E0E'>INTERNAL</text><text x='70' y='194' font-size='22' fill='#6B6B6B'>your own team uses it first</text><rect x='20' y='250' width='20' height='20' fill='#2F5FE8'/><text x='70' y='268' font-size='27' font-weight='500' fill='#0E0E0E'>CANARY · 5%</text><text x='70' y='304' font-size='22' fill='#6B6B6B'>watch errors and latency</text><rect x='20' y='360' width='20' height='20' fill='#2F5FE8'/><text x='70' y='378' font-size='27' font-weight='500' fill='#0E0E0E'>RAMP · 50%</text><text x='70' y='414' font-size='22' fill='#6B6B6B'>compare against the old path</text><rect x='20' y='470' width='20' height='20' fill='#2F5FE8'/><text x='70' y='488' font-size='27' font-weight='500' fill='#0E0E0E'>RELEASE · 100%</text><text x='70' y='524' font-size='22' fill='#6B6B6B'>everyone has it</text><rect x='20' y='580' width='20' height='20' fill='#0E0E0E'/><text x='70' y='598' font-size='27' font-weight='500' fill='#0E0E0E'>CLEAN UP</text><text x='70' y='634' font-size='22' fill='#6B6B6B'>delete the flag and the old code</text><line x1='560' y1='260' x2='790' y2='260' stroke='#2F5FE8' stroke-width='2' stroke-dasharray='8 7'/><line x1='560' y1='370' x2='790' y2='370' stroke='#2F5FE8' stroke-width='2' stroke-dasharray='8 7'/><line x1='560' y1='480' x2='790' y2='480' stroke='#2F5FE8' stroke-width='2' stroke-dasharray='8 7'/><line x1='790' y1='480' x2='790' y2='52' stroke='#2F5FE8' stroke-width='3' stroke-dasharray='8 7'/><path d='M778,66 L790,44 L802,66 Z' fill='#2F5FE8'/><line x1='0' y1='690' x2='850' y2='690' stroke='#D4D4D0' stroke-width='2'/><text x='0' y='738' font-size='24' font-weight='500' fill='#2F5FE8'>KILL SWITCH</text><text x='0' y='774' font-size='22' fill='#6B6B6B'>At any step: flag OFF in seconds. No redeploy.</text></g></svg>"
    },
    {
      "theme": "light",
      "tag": "Real-world example",
      "offset": 110,
      "html": "<div class='kicker'>Knight Capital · 1 August 2012</div><h2>Flags are powerful. Old flags are dangerous.</h2><div style='display:grid;grid-template-columns:190px 1fr;row-gap:22px;align-items:baseline'><span class='mono' style='font-size:24px;color:#6B6B6B'>THE DEBT</span><p style='font-size:31px;color:#0E0E0E'>Code unused since 2003 was never deleted.</p><span class='mono' style='font-size:24px;color:#6B6B6B'>THE REUSE</span><p style='font-size:31px;color:#0E0E0E'>A new feature reused the old code's flag.</p><span class='mono' style='font-size:24px;color:#6B6B6B'>THE DEPLOY</span><p style='font-size:31px;color:#0E0E0E'>One of eight servers missed the update.</p><span class='mono accent' style='font-size:24px'>THE COST</span><p style='font-size:31px;color:#0E0E0E'>45 minutes of unintended orders. A loss of more than $460 million.</p></div><hr style='margin:30px 0'><p style='font-size:30px'>Source: SEC order and press release, October 2013.</p>"
    },
    {
      "theme": "light",
      "tag": "Practical application",
      "offset": 110,
      "html": "<h2>Treat every flag as debt with a due date</h2><div style='display:grid;grid-template-columns:70px 1fr;row-gap:28px;align-items:baseline'><span class='mono accent' style='font-size:28px'>01</span><p style='font-size:32px'><b style='font-family:Space Grotesk'>One owner, one expiry date.</b> Set both when the flag is created.</p><span class='mono accent' style='font-size:28px'>02</span><p style='font-size:32px'><b style='font-family:Space Grotesk'>Never reuse a flag name.</b> A new behaviour gets a new flag.</p><span class='mono accent' style='font-size:28px'>03</span><p style='font-size:32px'><b style='font-family:Space Grotesk'>Removal is part of done.</b> The ticket closes when the flag and old path are gone.</p><span class='mono accent' style='font-size:28px'>04</span><p style='font-size:32px'><b style='font-family:Space Grotesk'>Test the kill switch.</b> Turn it off in staging before you trust it in production.</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "theme": "light",
      "tag": "Takeaways",
      "offset": 140,
      "html": "<h2>What to remember</h2><p class='mono' style='font-size:24px;color:#6B6B6B;letter-spacing:.06em'>TWO DECISIONS</p><p style='font-size:34px;color:#0E0E0E'>Engineering decides when code ships.</p><p style='font-size:30px;margin-top:6px'>Product and the business decide when users see it.</p><hr style='margin:28px 0'><p class='mono' style='font-size:24px;color:#6B6B6B;letter-spacing:.06em'>SMALLER RISK</p><p style='font-size:34px;color:#0E0E0E'>Release to 5% before 100%.</p><p style='font-size:30px;margin-top:6px'>Rollback becomes a switch, not a redeploy.</p><hr style='margin:28px 0'><p class='mono' style='font-size:24px;color:#6B6B6B;letter-spacing:.06em'>REAL COST</p><p style='font-size:34px;color:#0E0E0E'>Every flag is a branch in production.</p><p style='font-size:30px;margin-top:6px'>Delete it as soon as it has done its job.</p>"
    },
    {
      "theme": "dark",
      "tag": "Your turn",
      "offset": 190,
      "html": "<h2 style='font-size:76px'>How many flags in your codebase have no owner?</h2><p style='margin-top:30px'>And when did your team last delete one?</p><hr><p class='mono' style='font-size:28px;line-height:1.8'><span class='accent'>Save</span> this before your next launch plan.<br><span class='accent'>Follow</span> @techtaleswithabhi for delivery, architecture &amp; AI — without the hype.</p>",
      "footnote": "techtaleswithabhi.com"
    }
  ]
}
